00D2D5  1               ;
00D2D5  1               ; THIS ROUTINE IS USED TO ASCERTAIN THAT A GIVEN
00D2D5  1               ; NUMBER OF LOCS REMAIN AVAILABLE FOR THE STACK.
00D2D5  1               ;    THE CALL IS:
00D2D5  1               ;	LDAI	NUMBER OF 2-BYTE ENTRIES NEEDED.
00D2D5  1               ;	JSR	GETSTK
00D2D5  1               ;
00D2D5  1               ; THIS ROUTINE MUST BE CALLED BY ANY ROUTINE WHICH PUTS
00D2D5  1               ; AN ARBITRARY AMOUNT OF STUFF ON THE STACK,
00D2D5  1               ; I.E., ANY RECURSIVE ROUTINE LIKE "FRMEVL".
00D2D5  1               ; IT IS ALSO CALLED BY ROUTINES SUCH AS "GOSUB" AND "FOR"
00D2D5  1               ; WHICH MAKE PERMANENT ENTRIES ON THE STACK.
00D2D5  1               ;
00D2D5  1               ; ROUTINES WHICH MERELY USE AND FREE UP THE GUARANTEED
00D2D5  1               ; NUMLEV LOCATIONS NEED NOT CALL THIS.
00D2D5  1               ;
00D2D5  1               ;
00D2D5  1               ; ON EXIT:
00D2D5  1               ;    [A] AND [X] HAVE BEEN MODIFIED.
