00ED6F  1               ; SUBTTL	EXPONENTIATION FUNCTION.
00ED6F  1               ;FIRST SAVE THE ORIGINAL ARGUMENT AND MULTIPLY THE FAC BY
00ED6F  1               ;LOG2(E). THE RESULT IS USED TO DETERMINE IF OVERFLOW
00ED6F  1               ;WILL OCCUR SINCE EXP(X)=2^(X*LOG2(E)) WHERE
00ED6F  1               ;LOG2(E)=LOG(E) BASE 2. THEN SAVE THE INTEGER PART OF
00ED6F  1               ;THIS TO SCALE THE ANSWER AT THE END. SINCE
00ED6F  1               ;2^Y=2^INT(Y)*2^(Y-INT(Y)) AND 2^INT(Y) IS EASY TO COMPUTE.
00ED6F  1               ;NOW COMPUTE 2^(X*LOG2(E)-INT(X*LOG2(E)) BY
00ED6F  1               ;P(LN(2)*(INT(X*LOG2(E))+1)-X) WHERE P IS AN APPROXIMATION
00ED6F  1               ;POLYNOMIAL. THE RESULT IS THEN SCALED BY THE POWER OF 2
00ED6F  1               ;PREVIOUSLY SAVED.
00ED6F  1               
